                <pb facs="0861" n="850" xml:id="pg850"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.635 Neep/15: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-19T15:00:00-00:44">November 19, 1937—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. President today sent message to Legislature asking immediate consideration of
                    initialed Neep Agreement. Gave 11 reasons for favorable action. Said Government
                    first made overtures to company. Numerous amendments expected to be adopted
                    including provisions against undesirable participation. Swedish engineers have
                    arrived with three trucks and machinery. Promoters claim to have secured
                    necessary funds.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
